From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: MTP verify steps flagged by the caller

Batched serving with mtp_replay took every ubatch whose sequences all had at
most mtp_replay rows for an MTP verify step. A prefill that small (a short
prompt after a copied prefix with many drafts per step, or the last rows of a
long prefill split across passes) was then handled as a verify step: its rows
stayed uncommitted, or a sequence on a new cell aborted the process. The caller
now flags verify decodes with llama_set_mtp_verify(); the recurrent memory and
the Mamba2 graph follow the flag, and graph reuse compares it.

Upstream: not planned (batched serving path).

